// MINALOC (Ministry of Local Government) — three posts open on Rwanda's
// official recruitment portal (recruitment.mifotra.gov.rw) as of Nov 2026:
// Legal affairs specialist, LG Capacity Development Specialist and IDP
// Management Specialist (all Level 3.II, Post:1, Under Contract).
//
// Grounding notes (kept here for the content editors who maintain this file,
// not shown to candidates):
// - No live Nov 2026 posting text could be retrieved (the portal is an
//   app-encrypted SPA). All three titles have run before at MINALOC with the
//   same title and the same Level 3.II grade, so their real responsibilities,
//   qualifications and competencies are reused from those postings:
//     * Legal Affairs Specialist, MINALOC, Level 3.II, posted 27 Jun 2022,
//       deadline 05 Jul 2022 (greatrwandajobs.com /job-Legal-Affairs-Specialist
//       -job-at-Ministry-of-Local-Government-23816) — responsibilities, Bachelor's
//       /Master's-in-Law qualification and competency list are real text from
//       that posting.
//     * IDP Management Specialist, MINALOC, Level 3.II, posted ~Mar 2022,
//       deadline 30 Mar 2022 (greatrwandajobs.com /job-IDP-Management-Specialist
//       -job-at-Minaloc-21634) — responsibilities, qualifications and
//       competencies are real text from that posting. Crucially, on that
//       Ministry's own site, "IDP" there is NOT "internally displaced person" —
//       it is Rwanda's "Integrated Development Programme" (IDP Model Villages),
//       a settlement programme launched in 2010 (built on the 2008 Rural
//       Settlement Task Force) that moves households out of scattered or
//       disaster-prone settlement into planned villages with clustered housing,
//       schools, health posts, water/electricity and livelihood support. This
//       is confirmed by Rwanda Housing Authority's own programme page
//       (rha.gov.rw/program5) and by the posting's own duties ("IDP 11
//       pillars", "income generation"). Exams below use this real meaning.
//     * LG Capacity Development Specialist: an exact-title MINALOC posting
//       from 2019 (greatrwandajobs.com /job-LG-Capacity-Development-Specialist
//       -Job-at-MINISTRY-OF-LOCAL-GOVERNMENT...-10944) gives real duties
//       (proximity coaching for extreme-poverty households, performance
//       contracts, SPIU reporting). A closer, more recent relative — "Local
//       Government Capacity Development and System Strengthening Specialist",
//       MINALOC, Level 3.VI, posted 21 Nov 2024 (greatrwandajobs.com /job
//       -Local-Government-Capacity-Development-and-System-Strengthening
//       -Specialist...-39512) — supplies the modern duty list (capacity gap
//       analysis, Planning & Budgeting Call Circulars I/II, long-term
//       capacity-development plan) used alongside it.
// - Beyond the postings, content is grounded in verified Rwandan law/policy
//   facts: Law N°065/2021 of 09/10/2021 governing the District; Presidential
//   Order N°001/01 of 06/02/2023 on Sector/Cell/Village organisation; Law
//   N°45/2011 of 25/11/2011 governing contracts; the 2018 law on civil,
//   commercial, labour and administrative procedure; Law N°66/2018 regulating
//   labour; Rwanda's court structure (Supreme Court, Court of Appeal, High
//   Court, Intermediate Courts, Primary Courts, Commercial Courts); the
//   Rwanda Law Reform Commission's drafting mandate; the Rwanda Governance
//   Board's decentralisation/coaching mandate; LODA's financing/capacity role
//   under Law N°62/2013 (and Presidential Order N°071/01 of 09/12/2022);
//   MINEMA's disaster-management mandate and high-risk-zone relocation work;
//   and general civic facts (NST1 pillars, Ubudehe A–E, Imihigo, Umuganda,
//   Rwanda's 1 July–30 June financial year). Where no verified source exists,
//   questions draw on standard public-administration/legal practice rather
//   than invented Rwanda-specific "facts".
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

